{
  "description": "Type the errors every operation of this data plane can return, matched on the body's `/error/code`: the `{ error: { code } }` codes the Dev Center data plane answers for a missing pool, dev box, environment or environment definition, and a bad pool name (carried over from #976's client-level code map). Declared on the service shape, so each operation's error union carries them. These codes mean something else at ARM (`AuthenticationFailed`, `ModelNotFound`, `PoolNotFound`), so they cannot go in the client-level `AZURE_ERROR_CODE_MAP`.",
  "patches": [
